#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0125.1 expect=skipped domain=SE
#note "Requirements.Variables SKIP CHANNEL. All is [ETCD, SEUPDES] and describeVariablesMismatch is CONJUNCTIVE, returning on the FIRST entry the dataset does not carry; this fixture removes the SECOND entry, so a green skip proves the iteration reaches past the first. ETCD is present and holds UNPLAN, so without the gate the rule would be silent for a different reason -- the scenario converts that silence into an auditable skip. Unaffected by M3-D3."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
dataset SE label="Subject Elements"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
---
S1 | SE | SUBJ-001 | 1 | UNPLAN
---
